From af72ec58bd8cd6a8f743a94c20e76500c4e4fbde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: architecture review <review@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:59:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] T1 prototype: the typed Lead surface below transport,
 with an MCP (stdio) and a CLI adapter

A catalog (aew.surface.contract) of twelve built tools and one designed tool, each with a closed JSON Schema,
its primitives, its judgments and its operation class; a runner (aew.surface.run) that composes existing guarded
engine operations into stages with explicit stop and retry rules and returns a StageResult carrying the revision,
the completed steps, where a bundle stopped, and an ActionProjection (aew.surface.projection). Transports: an MCP
stdio server (aew lead mcp) that holds no credential and forwards lead.tool to the Lead broker, and aew lead tool,
the CLI form of the same contract. The Lead projection declares the server as OpenCode 2.0.18's schema spells it;
the capability probe checks that shape.

Architecture review thread T1 (AEW-reviews/architecture-dcd43f1). Prototype, not for merge as is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
