From 084e3fa4fd4a4191b3fa0215d5f42d5066c169b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: architecture review <review@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:44:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] T1 follow-up: the Lead projection's MCP server runs with
 Code Mode off

OpenCode 2.0.18 puts MCP servers behind Code Mode by default: the model receives an `execute` JavaScript tool and a
partial catalog in its instructions, never the server's tools as function tools. A live probe against the real
binary (AEW-reviews/architecture-dcd43f1/T9-live-probe-1-results.md) showed the twelve `aew_*` tools absent from the
model request until the server entry set `codemode: false`; with it, all twelve are function tools (11,178 bytes).
The capability probe now requires the `codemode` key in Mcp.LocalConfigEncoded; the Lead golden is regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
